 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Embroidery is the art of decorating fabric with needle and thread (or yarn), making patterns and pictures with stitches.\nClassification:\n• traditional embroidery: hand-made designs passed down in a culture, often with symbolic meaning — for example the embroidered gowns of the North West (toghu) and the Bamoun and Fulani designs;\n• modern embroidery: machine embroidery, logos on uniforms and caps, new designs and materials, computer-controlled machines.\nIt can also be classified by technique: surface embroidery (stitches on top of the fabric), counted-thread work (stitches counted on an even-weave fabric), white work (white thread on white fabric).\nUses: decorating clothes, table linen, cushions, wall hangings, school badges; income from selling embroidered articles.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "problem": "Is the logo stitched by machine on a school uniform an example of traditional or modern embroidery?",
  "steps": [
   "It is made by a machine, often from a computer design.",
   "So it is modern embroidery."
  ],
  "answer": "Modern embroidery.",
  "checks": []
 },
